## 3. Expectations Gap Theoretical Correction (Pillar 4)

In response to forensic quant review, the Expectations Gap in [`screener_service.py`](file:///d:/Projects/Stock_Watchlist_Hub/src/screener/screener_service.py#L235-L245) was mathematically refactored to prevent naive $(ROCE - g_{\text{implied}})$ distortion:
$$\text{Sustainable Compounding Rate } (g_s) = \text{ROIC} \times \text{Reinvestment Rate}$$
$$\text{Expectations Asymmetry Gap } (\%) = g_s - g_{\text{implied}}$$
- **Validation Test:** Added [`test_expectations_gap_uses_sustainable_growth()`](file:///d:/Projects/Stock_Watchlist_Hub/tests/test_screener_service.py#L126-L142).
- **Empirical Impact on Live Screen:** For mature cash-cows like `CASTROLIND` (72.6% ROCE, low reinvestment), the asymmetry gap correctly contracted from an absurdly inflated $+64.7\%$ down to an economically accurate **$+6.6\%$**.

