### B. Walk-Forward Temporal Partitioning & Stability

Implemented 3-Fold Walk-Forward Rolling Evaluation in [`scripts/walk_forward_backtest_runner.py`](file:///d:/Projects/Stock_Watchlist_Hub/scripts/walk_forward_backtest_runner.py). 

> [!NOTE]
> **Mathematical Invariant on Degradation Ratio:**
> The classic degradation ratio $E[R_{\text{OOS}}] / E[R_{\text{IS}}]$ is mathematically meaningful only when In-Sample expectancy is positive ($E[R_{\text{IS}}] > 0$). When $E[R_{\text{IS}}] \le 0$, dividing yields sign distortions. We therefore report both raw $\Delta R = E[R_{\text{OOS}}] - E[R_{\text{IS}}]$ and the positive-only ratio.

- **Fold 1:** Train H2 2025 $\to$ Validate H1 2026:
  - $E[R_{\text{IS}}] = -0.20R \to E[R_{\text{OOS}}] = +0.13R$ ($\Delta R = \mathbf{+0.33R}$, Ratio: N/A due to $E[R_{\text{IS}}] \le 0$).
- **Fold 2:** Train through May 2026 $\to$ Validate Summer 2026:
  - $E[R_{\text{IS}}] = +0.02R \to E[R_{\text{OOS}}] = +0.31R$ ($\Delta R = \mathbf{+0.29R}$, Degradation Ratio: $15.5x$).
- **Fold 3:** Calibration Base 2025 $\to$ 2026 Full Out-of-Sample Holdout:
  - $E[R_{\text{IS}}] = -0.20R \to E[R_{\text{OOS}}] = +0.22R$ ($\Delta R = \mathbf{+0.42R}$, Ratio: N/A).
- **VCP Subgroup Trajectory:** Out-of-sample expected return remained positive across all 3 folds (Fold 1: $+4.43R$, Fold 2: $+0.55R$, Fold 3: $+2.10R$).

**Walk-Forward Stability Verdict:** **PRELIMINARY STABILITY** — Out-of-sample expectancy remained positive across all 3 validation partitions ($\Delta R \ge 0$), but multi-year longitudinal expansion is required to confirm persistent edge.

